Wiring in main.js / game.js:
```js
import { AudioEngine } from './game/audio.js';
const audio = new AudioEngine(settings);
game.audio = audio;
if (!params.has('nomusic')) audio.startMusic(); // call once at startup; keep it running through title and game
game.on('settingsChanged', () => audio.setVolumes(game.settings.soundVolume, game.settings.musicVolume)); // or audio.setVolumes() if game.settings is the object passed to the constructor
// every frame, the title screen included (update() also schedules the music):
if (game.player) {
  const cam = player.getCameraState();
  audio.setListener(cam.x, cam.y, cam.z, cam.yaw);
  audio.setUnderwater(player.eyeInWater); // optional
}
audio.update(dt);
```

Unlocking needs nothing extra: ui.js already calls `audio.unlock()` on the first pointerdown, and the engine also arms its own capture-phase pointer and key listeners until the context runs. No AudioContext is created before a user gesture, so Chrome logs no autoplay warning. `startMusic()` called before unlock is remembered and starts once audio is unlocked. A hidden tab suspends the context and becoming visible resumes it, with the music continuing exactly where it was.

Every existing call site is supported with matching signatures:
- player.js: `playBlock('step'|'land', BLOCKS[id].sound, feet x, y, z)` and `play('hurt'|'death'|'swim'|'splash', { x, y, z, volume })`.
- interaction.js: `playBlock('hit'|'break'|'place', sound, block centre)`, including material 'water' for bucket scoop (break) and pour (place), and `play('break_tool', pos)`.
- ui.js: `unlock()` and `play('click')`.

Suggested calls for later waves:
- Item pickup: `play('pop', pos)`, with no pitch argument because the variation is built in.
- TNT: keep `const h = play('fuse', pos)`, call `h?.setPosition(...)` while the entity moves, then `play('explode', pos)`; the 64-block range is built in.
- Eating: `play('eat', pos)` every 4 ticks, then `play('burp', pos)`.
- Mobs: `play('pig'|'cow'|'sheep'|'chicken'|'zombie', pos)`; for hurt, `zombie_hurt` or the mob sound with `pitch: 1.3`; creeper uses `creeper_hiss` then `explode`.
- Flint and steel: `ignite`. Water meeting lava: `fizz`.

Debugging: `audio.musicStatus` returns { state, piece, position, nextIn }. The test page is tools/audio-test.html, with modes `?selfcheck=1`, `&big=1&dry=1&only=stone`, `?piano=1` and `?roll=7,42`. Full notes are in docs/notes/audio.md.
